 <SPAN class=3D"k">END PROGRAM</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Defined operators such as these are required for the expressions that =
are=20
allowed also in structure constructors (see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Derive=
d-data_types">Derived-data=20
types</A>):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE> <SPAN class=3D"n">str1</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">string</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">char1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">//</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">char2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
structure constructor</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Arrays_2">Arrays</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Arrays" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D25">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>In the case of arrays then, as long as they are of the same shape=20
(conformable), operations and assignments are extended in an obvious =
way, on an=20
element-by-element basis. For example, given declarations of</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE> <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">20</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>      <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">v</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">w</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"kt">LOGICAL                    </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">flag</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">20</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>it can be written:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN>                                       <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! whole array assignment</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN> =
                                    <SPAN class=3D"c">! whole array =
division and assignment</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">0.</SPAN>                                      <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! whole array assignment of scalar value</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"n">w</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">v</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">1.</SPAN>                                  <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! whole array addition to scalar value</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"n">w</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">v</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                         =
<SPAN class=3D"c">! array division, and addition to section</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"n">flag</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN>                                 <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
whole array relational test and assignment</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">8</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">9</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">8</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">15</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">20</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
array section addition and assignment</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"n">v</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">v</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                             <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
overlapping section assignment</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The order of expression evaluation is not specified in order to allow =
for=20
optimization on parallel and vector machines. Of course, any operators =
for=20
arrays of derived type must be defined.</P>
<P>Some real intrinsic functions that are useful for numeric =
computations=20
are</P>
<PRE>CEILING         FLOOR         MODULO (also integer)=0A=
EXPONENT        FRACTION=0A=
NEAREST         RRSPACING     SPACING=0A=
SCALE           SET_EXPONENT=0A=
</PRE>
<P>These are array valued for array arguments (elemental), like all <A =
title=3D"FORTRAN 77"=20
class=3D"mw-redirect" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FORTRAN_77">FORTRAN=20
77</A> functions (except LEN):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE> <SPAN class=3D"nb">INT             </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL  =
        </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">CMPLX</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> AINT            ANINT         NINT</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> ABS             MOD           SIGN</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> DIM             MAX           MIN</SPAN>=0A=
=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> SQRT            EXP           LOG</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">LOG10</SPAN>           =
<SPAN class=3D"nb">SIN           COS</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> TAN             ASIN          ACOS</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> ATAN            </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">ATAN2</SPAN>=0A=
 <SPAN class=3D"nb">SINH            COSH          TANH</SPAN>=0A=
=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> AIMAG           CONJG</SPAN>=0A=
=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> LGE             LGT           LLE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> LLT             ICHAR         CHAR</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb"> INDEX</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>(the last seven are for characters).</P>
<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Control_statements">Control=20
statements</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Control statements" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D26">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Branching_and_conditions">Branching and=20
conditions</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Branching and conditions" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D27">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>The simple <CODE>GO TO</CODE> <I>label</I> exists, but is usually =
avoided =E2=80=94=20
in most cases, a more specific branching construct will accomplish the =
same=20
logic with more clarity.</P>
<P>The simple conditional test is the <CODE>IF</CODE> statement:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>A full-blown <CODE>IF</CODE> construct is illustrated by</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">&lt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">         IF</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">&lt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">            </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">0.</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"k">ELSE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">            </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">z</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">0.</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"k">END IF</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">      ELSE IF</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">k</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">&lt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">         </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">z</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">1.</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">ELSE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">         </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">1.</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">END IF</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"CASE_construct">CASE =
construct</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: CASE =
construct"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D28">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>The <CODE>CASE</CODE> construct is a replacement for the computed=20
<CODE>GOTO</CODE>, but is better structured and does not require the use =
of=20
statement labels:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">SELECT CASE</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">number</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>       <SPAN class=3D"c">! number of type =
integer</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">CASE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                 <SPAN class=3D"c">! all values =
below 0</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"n">n_sign</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">CASE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                   <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! only 0</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"n">n_sign</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"mi">0</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">CASE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:)</SPAN>                  <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! all values above 0</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"n">n_sign</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">END SELECT</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Each <CODE>CASE</CODE> selector list may contain a list and/or range =
of=20
integers, character or logical constants, whose values may not overlap =
within or=20
between selectors:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">CASE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">7</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">17</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">23</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>A default is available:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">CASE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">DEFAULT</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>There is only one evaluation, and only one match.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"DO_construct">DO =
construct</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: DO =
construct"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D29">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>A simplified but sufficient form of the <CODE>DO</CODE> construct is=20
illustrated by</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"n">outer</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DO</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">   </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">inner</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN>    <SPAN class=3D"k">DO </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">k</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">l</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"c">! from j to k in steps of l =
(l is optional)</SPAN>=0A=
                <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
                <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(...)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">CYCLE</SPAN>=0A=
                <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
                <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(...)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">EXIT </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">outer</SPAN>=0A=
             <SPAN class=3D"k">END DO </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">inner</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"k">END DO </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">outer</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>where we note that loops may be optionally named so that any EXIT or =
CYCLE=20
statement may specify which loop is meant.</P>
<P>Many, but not all, simple loops can be replaced by array expressions =
and=20
assignments, or by new intrinsic functions. For instance</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"n">tot</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"mf">0.</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"k">DO </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">m</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN>=0A=
             <SPAN class=3D"n">tot</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">tot</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"k">END DO</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>becomes simply</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"n">tot</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"nb">SUM</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">m</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Program_units_and_procedures">Program units=20
and procedures</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Program units and procedures" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D30">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Definitions">Definitions</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Definitions"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D31">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>In order to discuss this topic we need some definitions. In logical =
terms, an=20
executable program consists of one <I>main program</I> and zero or more=20
<I>subprograms</I> (or <I>procedures</I>) - these do something. =
Subprograms are=20
either <I>functions</I> or <I>subroutines</I>, which are either =
<I>external,=20
internal</I> or <I>module</I> subroutines. (External subroutines are =
what we=20
knew from FORTRAN 77.)</P>
<P>From an organizational point of view, however, a complete program =
consists of=20
<I>program units</I>. These are either <I>main programs, external</I>=20
subprograms <I>or</I> modules <I>and can be separately compiled.</I></P>
<P>An example of a main (and complete) program is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">PROGRAM </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">test</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">PRINT</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s1">'Hello world!'</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">END PROGRAM </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">test</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>An example of a main program and an external subprogram, forming an=20
executable program, is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">PROGRAM </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">test</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">CALL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">print_message</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">END PROGRAM </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">test</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">print_message</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">PRINT</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s1">'Hello world!'</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">END SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">print_message</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The form of a function is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">name</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">arg1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">arg2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
zero or more arguments</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>                     =0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">name</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">...</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">name</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The form of reference of a function is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">name</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Internal_procedures">Internal=20
procedures</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Internal procedures" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D32">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>An internal subprogram is one <I>contained</I> in another (at a =
maximum of=20
one level of nesting) and provides a replacement for the statement =
function:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">outer</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">CONTAINS</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">        SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">inner</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">1.</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">inner</SPAN>     <SPAN class=3D"c">! SUBROUTINE =
mandatory</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">outer</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>We say that <CODE>outer</CODE> is the <I>host</I> of =
<CODE>inner</CODE>, and=20
that <CODE>inner</CODE> obtains access to entities in <CODE>outer</CODE> =
by=20
<I>host association</I> (e.g. to <CODE>x</CODE>), whereas <CODE>y</CODE> =
is a=20
<I>local</I> variable to <CODE>inner</CODE>.</P>
<P>The <I>scope</I> of a named entity is a <I>scoping unit</I>, here=20
<CODE>outer</CODE> less <CODE>inner</CODE>, and <CODE>inner</CODE>.</P>
<P>The names of program units and external procedures are <I>global</I>, =
and the=20
names of implied-DO variables have a scope of the statement that =
contains=20
them.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Modules">Modules</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Modules" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D33">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Modules are used to package</P>
<UL>
  <LI>global data (replaces COMMON and BLOCK DATA from Fortran 77);</LI>
  <LI>type definitions (themselves a scoping unit);</LI>
  <LI>subprograms (which among other things replaces the use of ENTRY =
from=20
  Fortran 77);</LI>
  <LI>interface blocks (another scoping unit, see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Interf=
ace_blocks">Interface=20
  blocks</A>);</LI>
  <LI>namelist groups (see any textbook).</LI></UL>
<P>An example of a module containing a type definition, interface block =
and=20
function subprogram is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">MODULE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">interval_arithmetic</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">interval</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">lower</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">upper</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END TYPE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">interval</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">INTERFACE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">OPERATOR</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"k">MODULE PROCEDURE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">add_intervals</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END INTERFACE</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">CONTAINS</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">        FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">add_intervals</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">interval</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">IN</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">interval</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">add_intervals</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"n">add_intervals</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">lower</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">lower</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">lower</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"n">add_intervals</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">upper</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">upper</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">upper</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">add_intervals</SPAN>             <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
FUNCTION mandatory</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END MODULE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">interval_arithmetic</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and the simple statement</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     =0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">USE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">interval_arithmetic</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>provides <I>use association</I> to all the module's entities. Module=20
subprograms may, in turn, contain internal subprograms.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Controlling_accessibility">Controlling=20
accessibility</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Controlling accessibility" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D34">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>The <CODE>PUBLIC</CODE> and <CODE>PRIVATE</CODE> attributes are used =
in=20
specifications in modules to limit the scope of entities. The attribute =
form=20
is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">PUBLIC</SPAN>     <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">z</SPAN>           <SPAN class=3D"c">! default</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">PRIVATE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">v</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">w</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and the statement form is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">PUBLIC</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">z</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">OPERATOR</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">add</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">.)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">PRIVATE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">v</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">w</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">ASSIGNMENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">OPERATOR</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The statement form has to be used to limit access to operators, and =
can also=20
be used to change the overall default:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">PRIVATE</SPAN>                        <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! sets default for module</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">PUBLIC</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">only_this</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>For derived types there are three possibilities: the type and its =
components=20
are all PUBLIC, the type is PUBLIC and its components PRIVATE (the type =
only is=20
visible and one can change its details easily), or all of it is PRIVATE =
(for=20
internal use in the module only):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">MODULE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">mine</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">PRIVATE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">        TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">PUBLIC</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">list</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">list</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">next</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END TYPE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">list</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">list</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">tree</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END MODULE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">mine</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The <CODE>USE</CODE> statement's purpose is to gain access to =
entities in a=20
module. It has options to resolve name clashes if an imported name is =
the same=20
as a local one:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">USE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">mine</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">local_list</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">list</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>or to restrict the used entities to a specified set:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">USE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">mine</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">ONLY</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">list</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>These may be combined:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">USE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">mine</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">ONLY</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">local_list</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">list</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Arguments">Arguments</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Arguments" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D35">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>We may specify the intent of dummy arguments:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">shuffle</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ncards</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">cards</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">IN</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">ncards</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">OUT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ncards</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">cards</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Also, INOUT is possible: here the actual argument must be a variable =
(unlike=20
the default case where it may be a constant).</P>
<P>Arguments may be optional:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">mincon</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">upper</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">lower</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">equalities</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">inequalities</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">convex</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">xstart</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">OPTIONAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">upper</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">lower</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">PRESENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">lower</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>   <SPAN class=3D"c">! test for presence of =
actual argument</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>allows us to call <CODE>mincon</CODE> by</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>        <SPAN class=3D"k">CALL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">mincon</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">upper</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Arguments may be keyword rather than positional (which come =
first):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>        <SPAN class=3D"k">CALL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">mincon</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">equalities</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">xstart</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Optional and keyword arguments are handled by explicit interfaces, =
that is=20
with internal or module procedures or with interface blocks.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Interface_blocks">Interface =
blocks</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Interface blocks"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D36">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Any reference to an internal or module subprogram is through an =
interface=20
that is 'explicit' (that is, the compiler can see all the details). A =
reference=20
to an external (or dummy) procedure is usually 'implicit' (the compiler =
assumes=20
the details). However, we can provide an explicit interface in this case =
too. It=20
is a copy of the header, specifications and END statement of the =
procedure=20
concerned, either placed in a module or inserted directly:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">FUNCTION =
</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">minimum</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">func</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">! returns the minimum value of the function =
func(x)</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">! in the interval (a,b)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">in</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">INTERFACE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">           </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">func</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
              <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">IN</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">func</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END INTERFACE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">        </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">f</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">func</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>   <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
invocation of the user function.</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">minimum</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>An explicit interface is obligatory for</P>
<UL>
  <LI>optional and keyword arguments;</LI>
  <LI>POINTER and TARGET arguments (see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Pointe=
rs">Pointers</A>);</LI>
  <LI>POINTER function result;</LI>
  <LI>new-style array arguments and array functions (<A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Array_=
handling">Array=20
  handling</A>).</LI></UL>
<P>It allows full checks at compile time between actual and dummy =
arguments.</P>
<P><B>In general, the best way to ensure that a procedure interface is =
explicit=20
is either to place the procedure concerned in a module or to use it as =
an=20
internal procedure.</B></P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline"=20
id=3D"Overloading_and_generic_interfaces">Overloading and generic=20
interfaces</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Overloading and generic interfaces" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D37">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Interface blocks provide the mechanism by which we are able to define =
generic=20
names for specific procedures:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">INTERFACE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">gamma</SPAN>                   <SPAN class=3D"c">! generic =
name</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">sgamma</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">X</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>             <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! specific name</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">SELECTED_REAL_KIND</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">6</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">sgamma</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">        FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">dgamma</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">X</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>             <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! specific name</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">SELECTED_REAL_KIND</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">12</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">dgamma</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">     END INTERFACE</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>where a given set of specific names corresponding to a generic name =
must all=20
be of functions or all of subroutines. If this interface is within a =
module,=20
then it is simply</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">INTERFACE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">gamma</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb">        </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">MODULE PROCEDURE =
</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">sgamma</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">dgamma</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END INTERFACE</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>We can use existing names, e.g. SIN, and the compiler sorts out the =
correct=20
association.</P>
<P>We have already seen the use of interface blocks for defined =
operators and=20
assignment (see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Module=
s">Modules</A>).</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Recursion">Recursion</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Recursion" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D38">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Indirect recursion is useful for multi-dimensional integration. =
For</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"n">volume</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">integrate</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">fy</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">ybounds</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>We might have</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">RECURSIVE FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">integrate</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">bounds</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"c">! Integrate f(x) from bounds(1) to =
bounds(2)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">integrate</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">INTERFACE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">           FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
              <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END INTERFACE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">        </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">IN</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">bounds</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">integrate</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and to integrate <I>f(x, y)</I> over a rectangle:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">fy</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">USE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">func</SPAN>       =
    <SPAN class=3D"c">! module func contains function f</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">fy</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">yval</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">fy</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">integrate</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">xbounds</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Direct recursion is when a procedure calls itself, as in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">RECURSIVE FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">factorial</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">RESULT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">res</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">res</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">EQ</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">           </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">res</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">ELSE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">           </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">res</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">factorial</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END IF</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">     END</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Here, we note the <CODE>RESULT</CODE> clause and termination =
test.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Pure_Procedures">Pure =
Procedures</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: Pure =
Procedures"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D39">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>This is a feature for parallel computing.</P>
<P>In <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#The_FO=
RALL_Statement_and_Construct">the=20
FORALL Statement and Construct</A>, any side effects in a function can =
impede=20
optimization on a parallel processor=E2=80=94the order of execution of =
the assignments=20
could affect the results. To control this situation, we add the=20
<CODE>PURE</CODE> keyword to the <CODE>SUBROUTINE</CODE> or=20
<CODE>FUNCTION</CODE> statement=E2=80=94an assertion that the procedure =
(expressed=20
simply):</P>
<UL>
  <LI>alters no global variable,</LI>
  <LI>performs no I/O,</LI>
  <LI>has no saved variables (variables with the <CODE>SAVE</CODE> =
attribute=20
  that retains values between invocations), and</LI>
  <LI>for functions, does not alter any of its arguments.</LI></UL>
<P>A compiler can check that this is the case, as in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">PURE FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">calculate</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>All the intrinsic functions are pure.</P>
<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Array_handling">Array =
handling</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: Array =
handling"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D40">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<P>Array handling is included in Fortran for two main reasons:</P>
<UL>
  <LI>the notational convenience it provides, bringing the code closer =
to the=20
  underlying mathematical form;</LI>
  <LI>for the additional optimization opportunities it gives compilers =
(although=20
  there are plenty of opportunities for degrading optimization =
too!).</LI></UL>
<P>At the same time, major extensions of the functionality in this area =
have=20
been added. We have already met whole arrays <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Arrays=
_1">above</A>=20
and <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Arrays=
_2">here</A>=20
- now we develop the theme.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Zero-sized_arrays">Zero-sized=20
arrays</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Zero-sized arrays"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D41">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>A zero-sized array is handled by Fortran as a legitimate object, =
without=20
special coding by the programmer. Thus, in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">DO </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">*</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END DO</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>no special code is required for the final iteration where <CODE>i =3D =
n</CODE>.=20
We note that a zero-sized array is regarded as being defined; however, =
an array=20
of shape (0,2) is not conformable with one of shape (0,3), whereas</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>    <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">3</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>is a valid 'do nothing' statement.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Assumed-shape_arrays">Assumed-shape=20
arrays</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Assumed-shape arrays"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D42">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>These are an extension and replacement for assumed-size arrays. Given =
an=20
actual argument like:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">20</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">CALL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">sub</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>the corresponding dummy argument specification defines only the type =
and rank=20
of the array, not its shape. This information has to be made available =
by an=20
explicit interface, often using an interface block (see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Interf=
ace_blocks">Interface=20
blocks</A>). Thus we write just</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>  <SPAN class=3D"k">SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">sub</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">da</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">:)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">da</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and this is as if <CODE>da</CODE> were dimensioned (11,21). However, =
we can=20
specify any lower bound and the array maps accordingly.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">da</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The shape, not bounds, is passed, where the default lower bound is 1 =
and the=20
default upper bound is the corresponding extent.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Automatic_arrays">Automatic =
arrays</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Automatic arrays"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D43">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>A partial replacement for the uses to which <CODE>EQUIVALENCE</CODE> =
was put=20
is provided by this facility, useful for local, temporary arrays, as =
in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">swap</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN>       <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">SIZE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">work</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">work</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">work</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">swap</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The actual storage is typically maintained on a stack.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"ALLOCATABLE_and_ALLOCATE">ALLOCATABLE and=20
ALLOCATE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
ALLOCATABLE and ALLOCATE"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D44">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Fortran provides dynamic allocation of storage; it relies on a heap =
storage=20
mechanism (and replaces another use of <CODE>EQUIVALENCE</CODE>). An =
example,=20
for establishing a work array for a whole program, is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">MODULE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">work_array</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:,:,:),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">ALLOCATABLE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">work</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END MODULE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">     PROGRAM </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">main</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">USE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">work_array</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">READ</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">input</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">ALLOCATE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">work</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"nb">STAT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">status</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">DEALLOCATE</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">work</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The work array can be propagated through the whole program via a=20
<CODE>USE</CODE> statement in each program unit. We may specify an =
explicit=20
lower bound and allocate several entities in one statement. To free dead =
storage=20
we write, for instance,</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">DEALLOCATE</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Deallocation of arrays is automatic when they go out of scope.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Elemental_operations.2C_assignments_and_procedures">Elemental=20
operations, assignments and procedures</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Elemental operations, assignments and procedures"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D45">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>We have already met whole array assignments and operations:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">0.</SPAN>          <SPAN class=3D"c">! scalar broadcast; =
elemental assignment</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"nb">SQRT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>     <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
intrinsic function result as array object</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>In the second assignment, an intrinsic function returns an =
array-valued=20
result for an array-valued argument. We can write array-valued functions =

ourselves (they require an explicit interface):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">PROGRAM </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">test</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">1.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">2.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">3.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN>       <SPAN =
class=3D"p">&amp;</SPAN>=0A=
                            <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">2.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">2.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">2.</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"n">r</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">r</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">PRINT</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">r</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">CONTAINS</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">      FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">f</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">d</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">d</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">SIZE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">f</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">f</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">d</SPAN> =
       <SPAN class=3D"c">! (or some more useful function of c and =
d)</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">f</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">END PROGRAM </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">test</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Elemental procedures are specified with scalar dummy arguments that =
may be=20
called with array actual arguments. In the case of a function, the shape =
of the=20
result is the shape of the array arguments.</P>
<P>Most intrinsic functions are elemental and Fortran 95 extends this =
feature to=20
non-intrinsic procedures, thus providing the effect of writing, in =
Fortran 90,=20
22 different versions, for ranks 0-0, 0-1, 1-0, 1-1, 0-2, 2-0, 2-2, ... =
7-7, and=20
is further an aid to optimization on parallel processors. An elemental =
procedure=20
must be pure.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">ELEMENTAL SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">swap</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">INOUT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN>                 <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">work</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">work</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">work</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">END SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">swap</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The dummy arguments cannot be used in specification expressions (see =
<A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Specif=
ication_expressions">above</A>)=20
except as arguments to certain intrinsic functions =
(<CODE>BIT_SIZE</CODE>,=20
<CODE>KIND</CODE>, <CODE>LEN</CODE>, and the numeric inquiry ones, (see =
<A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Intrin=
sic_data_types">below</A>).</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"WHERE">WHERE</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
WHERE" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D46">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Often, we need to mask an assignment. This we can do using the=20
<CODE>WHERE</CODE>, either as a statement:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">WHERE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">/=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">0.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">1.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"c">! avoid division by 0</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>(note: the test is element-by-element, not on whole array), or as a=20
construct:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">WHERE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">/=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">0.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">1.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>             <SPAN class=3D"c">! all arrays same =
shape</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END WHERE</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>or</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">WHERE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">/=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">0.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">1.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"n">ELSEWHERE</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"nb">HUGE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END WHERE</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Further:</P>
<UL>
  <LI>it is permitted to mask not only the <CODE>WHERE</CODE> statement =
of the=20
  <CODE>WHERE</CODE> construct, but also any <CODE>ELSEWHERE</CODE> =
statement=20
  that it contains;</LI>
  <LI>a <CODE>WHERE</CODE> construct may contain any number of masked=20
  <CODE>ELSEWHERE</CODE> statements but at most one =
<CODE>ELSEWHERE</CODE>=20
  statement without a mask, and that must be the final one;</LI>
  <LI><CODE>WHERE</CODE> constructs may be nested within one another, =
just=20
  <CODE>FORALL</CODE> constructs;</LI>
  <LI>a <CODE>WHERE</CODE> assignment statement is permitted to be a =
defined=20
  assignment, provided that it is elemental;</LI>
  <LI>a <CODE>WHERE</CODE> construct may be named in the same way as =
other=20
  constructs.</LI></UL>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"The_FORALL_Statement_and_Construct">The FORALL=20
Statement and Construct</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: The FORALL Statement and Construct" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D47">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>When a <CODE>DO</CODE> construct is executed, each successive =
iteration is=20
performed in order and one after the other=E2=80=94an impediment to =
optimization on a=20
parallel processor.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">FORALL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>where the individual assignments may be carried out in any order, and =
even=20
simultaneously. The <CODE>FORALL</CODE> may be considered to be an array =

assignment expressed with the help of indices.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">FORALL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mf">0.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">1.0</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>with masking condition.</P>
<P>The <CODE>FORALL</CODE> construct allows several assignment =
statements to be=20
executed in order.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>is equivalent to the array assignments</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">FORALL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">END FORALL</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The <CODE>FORALL</CODE> version is more readable.</P>
<P>Assignment in a <CODE>FORALL</CODE> is like an array assignment: as =
if all=20
the expressions were evaluated in any order, held in temporary storage, =
then all=20
the assignments performed in any order. The first statement must fully =
complete=20
before the second can begin.</P>
<P>A <CODE>FORALL</CODE> may be nested, and may include a =
<CODE>WHERE</CODE>.=20
Procedures referenced within a <CODE>FORALL</CODE> must be pure.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Array_elements">Array =
elements</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: Array =
elements"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D48">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>For a simple case, given</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>         <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">100</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">100</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>we can reference a single element as, for instance, <CODE>a(1, =
1)</CODE>. For=20
a derived-data type like</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">fun_del</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL                  </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">du</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END TYPE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">fun_del</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>we can declare an array of that type:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">fun_del</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">20</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and a reference like</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>                     <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>is an element (a scalar!) of type fun_del, but</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>                     <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">du</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>is an array of type real, and</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>                     <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">du</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>is an element of it. The basic rule to remember is that an array =
element=20
always has a subscript or subscripts qualifying at least the last =
name.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Array_subobjects_.28sections.29">Array=20
subobjects (sections)</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Array subobjects (sections)" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D49">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>The general form of subscript for an array section is</P>
<PRE>      [<I>lower</I>] : [<I>upper</I>] [:<I>stride</I>]=0A=
</PRE>
<P>(where [ ] indicates an optional item) as in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>       <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! part of one row</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">m</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! part of one column</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                 <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! whole row</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>              <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! every third element of row</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">-</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>            <SPAN class=3D"c">! row in reverse =
order</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">7</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"c">! vector subscript</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">11</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>             <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! 11 is legal as not referenced</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">7</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! rank two section</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Note that a vector subscript with duplicate values cannot appear on =
the=20
left-hand side of an assignment as it would be ambiguous. Thus,</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>       <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">7</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">7</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">4</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>is illegal. Also, a section with a vector subscript must not be =
supplied as=20
an actual argument to an <CODE>OUT</CODE> or <CODE>INOUT</CODE> dummy =
argument.=20
Arrays of arrays are not allowed:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>       <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">du</SPAN>             <SPAN class=3D"c">! illegal</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>We note that a given value in an array can be referenced both as an =
element=20
and as a section:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>            <SPAN =
class=3D"c">!  scalar (rank zero)</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>          <SPAN =
class=3D"c">!  array section (rank one)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>depending on the circumstances or requirements. By qualifying objects =
of=20
derived type, we obtain elements or sections depending on the rule =
stated=20
earlier:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>       <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN>              <SPAN class=3D"c">!  array section =
(structure component)</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN>        <SPAN class=3D"c">!  component of an array =
element</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Arrays_intrinsic_functions">Arrays =
intrinsic=20
functions</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Arrays intrinsic functions" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D50">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P><I><B>Vector and matrix multiply</B></I></P>
<PRE>     DOT_PRODUCT        Dot product of 2 rank-one arrays=0A=
     MATMUL             Matrix multiplication=0A=
</PRE>
<P><I><B>Array reduction</B></I></P>
<PRE>     ALL                True if all values are true=0A=
     ANY                True if any value is true. Example:=0A=
                            IF (ANY( a &gt; b)) THEN=0A=
     COUNT              Number of true elements in array=0A=
     MAXVAL             Maximum value in an array=0A=
     MINVAL             Minimum value in an array=0A=
     PRODUCT            Product of array elements=0A=
     SUM                Sum of array elements=0A=
</PRE>
<P><I><B>Array inquiry</B></I></P>
<PRE>     ALLOCATED          Array allocation status=0A=
     LBOUND             Lower dimension bounds of an array=0A=
     SHAPE              Shape of an array (or scalar)=0A=
     SIZE               Total number of elements in an array=0A=
     UBOUND             Upper dimension bounds of an array=0A=
</PRE>
<P><I><B>Array construction</B></I></P>
<PRE>     MERGE              Merge under mask=0A=
     PACK               Pack an array into an array of rank one under a =
mask=0A=
     SPREAD             Replicate array by adding a dimension=0A=
     UNPACK             Unpack an array of rank one into an array under =
mask=0A=
</PRE>
<P><I><B>Array reshape</B></I></P>
<PRE>     RESHAPE            Reshape an array=0A=
</PRE>
<P><I><B>Array manipulation</B></I></P>
<PRE>     CSHIFT             Circular shift=0A=
     EOSHIFT            End-off shift=0A=
     TRANSPOSE          Transpose of an array of rank two=0A=
</PRE>
<P><I><B>Array location</B></I></P>
<PRE>     MAXLOC             Location of first maximum value in an array=0A=
     MINLOC             Location of first minimum value in an array=0A=
</PRE>
<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Pointers">Pointers</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Pointers" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D51">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Basics_2">Basics</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Basics" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D52">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Pointers are variables with the <CODE>POINTER</CODE> attribute; they =
are not=20
a distinct data type (and so no 'pointer arithmetic' is possible).</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">var</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>They are conceptually a descriptor listing the attributes of the =
objects=20
(targets) that the pointer may point to, and the address, if any, of a =
target.=20
They have no associated storage until it is allocated or otherwise =
associated=20
(by pointer assignment, see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Pointe=
rs_in_expressions_and_assignments">below</A>):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"k">ALLOCATE</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">var</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and they are dereferenced automatically, so no special symbol =
required.=20
In</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"n">var</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">var</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mf">2.3</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>the value of the target of var is used and modified. Pointers cannot =
be=20
transferred via I/O. The statement</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"k">WRITE</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">var</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>writes the value of the target of var and not the pointer descriptor=20
itself.</P>
<P>A pointer can point to another pointer, and hence to its target, or =
to a=20
static object that has the <CODE>TARGET</CODE> attribute:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">object</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">TARGET</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">target_obj</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"n">var</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">object</SPAN>                  <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
pointer assignment</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"n">var</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">target_obj</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>but they are strongly typed:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">int_var</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"n">var</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">int_var</SPAN>                 <SPAN class=3D"c">! =
illegal - types must match</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and, similarly, for arrays the ranks as well as the type must =
agree.</P>
<P>A pointer can be a component of a derived type:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>        <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE entry</SPAN>                       =
<SPAN class=3D"c">! type for sparse matrix</SPAN>=0A=
           <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">value</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">           </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER =
</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">index</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb">           </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">entry</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">next</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! note recursion</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">END TYPE entry</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and we can define the beginning of a linked chain of such =
entries:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>        <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">entry</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">chain</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>After suitable allocations and definitions, the first two entries =
could be=20
addressed as</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>        <SPAN class=3D"n">chain</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">value           </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">chain</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">next</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">value</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">        </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">chain</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">index           </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">chain</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">next</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">index</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb">        </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">chain</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">next</SPAN>            <SPAN =
class=3D"n">chain</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">next</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">next</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>but we would normally define additional pointers to point at, for =
instance,=20
the first and current entries in the list.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Association">Association</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Association"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D53">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>A pointer's association status is one of</P>
<DIV>
<UL>
  <LI>undefined (initial state);</LI>
  <LI>associated (after allocation or a pointer assignment);</LI>
  <LI>disassociated:=20
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"k">DEALLOCATE</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">q</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! for returning storage</SPAN>=0A=
          <SPAN class=3D"k">NULLIFY</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">q</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>     <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! for setting to 'null'</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV></LI></UL></DIV>
<P>Some care has to be taken not to leave a pointer 'dangling' by use of =

<CODE>DEALLOCATE</CODE> on its target without nullifying any other =
pointer=20
referring to it.</P>
<P>The intrinsic function <CODE>ASSOCIATED</CODE> can test the =
association=20
status of a defined pointer:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>               <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">ASSOCIATED</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">pointer</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>or between a defined pointer and a defined target (which may, itself, =
be a=20
pointer):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>               <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">ASSOCIATED</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"k">pointer</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">target</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>An alternative way to initialize a pointer, also in a specification=20
statement, is to use the <CODE>NULL</CODE> function:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">vector</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"nb">NULL</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">()</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"c">! compile time</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"n">vector</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"nb">NULL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">()</SPAN>                =
                <SPAN class=3D"c">! run time</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline"=20
id=3D"Pointers_in_expressions_and_assignments">Pointers in expressions =
and=20
assignments</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Pointers in expressions and assignments" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D54">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>For intrinsic types we can 'sweep' pointers over different sets of =
target=20
data using the same code without any data movement. Given the matrix=20
manipulation <I>y =3D B C z</I>, we can write the following code =
(although, in=20
this case, the same result could be achieved more simply by other =
means):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">TARGET</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">r</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">z</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:,:),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">mult</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">DO </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">mult</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"k">IF</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">mult</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">THEN</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">            </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">r</SPAN>              <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! no data movement</SPAN>=0A=
            <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN>=0A=
            <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">z</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"k">ELSE</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">            </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">s</SPAN>              <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! no data movement</SPAN>=0A=
            <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
            <SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">r</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"k">END IF</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">         </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"nb">MATMUL</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>       <SPAN =
class=3D"c">! common calculation</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">END DO</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>For objects of derived type we have to distinguish between pointer =
and normal=20
assignment. In</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">entry</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">first</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">current</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">first</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">current</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>the assignment causes first to point at current, whereas</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"n">first</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN>  =
<SPAN class=3D"n">current</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>causes current to overwrite first and is equivalent to</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"n">first</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">value</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">current</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">value</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">      </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">first</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">index</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">current</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">index</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"nb">      </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">first</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">next</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">current</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">next</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Pointer_arguments">Pointer=20
arguments</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Pointer arguments" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D55">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>If an actual argument is a pointer then, if the dummy argument is =
also a=20
pointer,</P>
<UL>
  <LI>it must have same rank,</LI>
  <LI>it receives its association status from the actual argument,</LI>
  <LI>it returns its final association status to the actual argument =
(note: the=20
  target may be undefined!),</LI>
  <LI>it may not have the <CODE>INTENT</CODE> attribute (it would be=20
  ambiguous),</LI>
  <LI>it requires an interface block.</LI></UL>
<P>If the dummy argument is not a pointer, it becomes associated with =
the target=20
of the actual argument:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(:,:)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">ALLOCATE</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">80</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">80</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">CALL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">sub</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
  <SPAN class=3D"k">SUBROUTINE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">sub</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(:,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">:)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Pointer_functions">Pointer=20
functions</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Pointer functions" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D56">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Function results may also have the <CODE>POINTER</CODE> attribute; =
this is=20
useful if the result size depends on calculations performed in the =
function, as=20
in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">USE </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">data_handler</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">100</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">compact</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>where the module data_handler contains</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">compact</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">compact</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN>=0A=
  <SPAN class=3D"c">! A procedure to remove duplicates from the array =
x</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>              <SPAN class=3D"c">! Find =
the number of distinct values, n</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">ALLOCATE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">compact</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>              <SPAN class=3D"c">! Copy =
the distinct values into compact</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">compact</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The result can be used in an expression (but must be associated with =
a=20
defined target).</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Arrays_of_pointers">Arrays of=20
pointers</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Arrays of pointers"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D57">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>These do not exist as such: given</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">entry</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">rows</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>then</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"n">rows</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">next</SPAN>              <SPAN class=3D"c">! illegal</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>would be such an object, but with an irregular storage pattern. For =
this=20
reason they are not allowed. However, we can achieve the same effect by =
defining=20
a derived data type with a pointer as its sole component:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">row</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">r</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:)</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END TYPE</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and then defining arrays of this data type</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">TYPE</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">row</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>where the storage for the rows can be allocated by, for instance,</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"k">DO </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN>=0A=
        <SPAN class=3D"k">ALLOCATE</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">r</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"c">! Allocate row i of length =
i</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"k">END DO</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The array assignment</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"n">s</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>is then equivalent to the pointer assignments</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">r</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">r</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>for all components.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Pointers_as_dynamic_aliases">Pointers as=20
dynamic aliases</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Pointers as dynamic aliases" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D58">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>Given an array</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>    <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">TARGET</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">table</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">100</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">100</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>that is frequently referenced with the fixed subscripts</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"n">table</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">m</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">q</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>these references may be replaced by</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>     <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(:,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">:),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">window</SPAN>=0A=
       <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
     <SPAN class=3D"n">window</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">table</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">m</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">q</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The subscripts of window are <CODE>1:n-m+1, 1:q-p+1</CODE>. =
Similarly,=20
for</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>           <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">u</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>(as defined in <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Array_=
elements">already</A>),=20
we can use, say,</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>           <SPAN class=3D"n">taru</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">tar</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">u</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>to point at all the u components of tar, and subscript it as</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>           <SPAN class=3D"n">taru</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The subscripts are as those of tar itself. (This replaces yet more of =

<CODE>EQUIVALENCE</CODE>.)</P>
<P>In the pointer association</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE><SPAN class=3D"k">pointer</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">array_expression</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>the lower bounds for <CODE>pointer</CODE> are determined as if=20
<CODE>lbound</CODE> was applied to <CODE>array_expression</CODE>. Thus, =
when a=20
pointer is assigned to a whole array variable, it inherits the lower =
bounds of=20
the variable, otherwise, the lower bounds default to 1. <A =
title=3D"Fortran 2003"=20
class=3D"mw-redirect" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_2003">Fortran=20
2003</A> allows specifying arbitrary lower bounds on pointer =
association,=20
like</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE><SPAN class=3D"n">window</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">r</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">table</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">m</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">q</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>so that the bounds of <CODE>window</CODE> become=20
<CODE>r:r+n-m,s:s+q-p</CODE>. <A title=3D"Fortran 95" =
class=3D"mw-redirect" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95">Fortran=20
95</A> does not have this feature; however, it can be simulated using =
the=20
following trick (based on the pointer association rules for assumed =
shape array=20
dummy arguments):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE><SPAN class=3D"k">FUNCTION </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">remap_bounds2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">lb1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">lb2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">array</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">RESULT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ptr</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">IN</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>                          =
  <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">lb1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">lb2</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">lb1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">lb2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">INTENT</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">IN</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">TARGET</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">array</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">   </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"kt">REAL</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">DIMENSION</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(:,:),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"k">POINTER</SPAN>               =
   <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">ptr</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"n">ptr</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">array</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"k">END FUNCTION</SPAN>=0A=
  <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">window</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D&gt;</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">remap_bounds2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">r</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">table</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">m</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">q</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The source code of an extended example of the use of pointers to =
support a=20
data structure is in <A class=3D"external text" =
href=3D"ftp://ftp.numerical.rl.ac.uk/pub/MRandC/pointer.f90"=20
rel=3D"nofollow">pointer.f90</A>.</P>
<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Intrinsic_procedures">Intrinsic=20
procedures</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Intrinsic procedures" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D59">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<P>Most of the intrinsic functions have already been mentioned. Here, we =
deal=20
only with their general classification and with those that have so far =
been=20
omitted. All intrinsic procedures can be used with keyword =
arguments:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>          <SPAN class=3D"k">CALL </SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">DATE_AND_TIME</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">TIME</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>and many have optional arguments.</P>
<P>The intrinsic procedures are grouped into four categories:</P>
<OL>
  <LI>elemental - work on scalars or arrays, e.g. =
<CODE>ABS(a)</CODE>;</LI>
  <LI>inquiry - independent of value of argument (which may be =
undefined), e.g.=20
  <CODE>PRECISION(a)</CODE>;</LI>
  <LI>transformational - array argument with array result of different =
shape,=20
  e.g. <CODE>RESHAPE(a, b)</CODE>;</LI>
  <LI>subroutines, e.g. <CODE>SYSTEM_CLOCK</CODE>.</LI></OL>
<P>The procedures not already introduced are</P>
<P>Bit inquiry</P>
<PRE>     BIT_SIZE           Number of bits in the model=0A=
=0A=
</PRE>
<P>Bit manipulation</P>
<PRE>     BTEST              Bit testing=0A=
     IAND               Logical AND=0A=
     IBCLR              Clear bit=0A=
     IBITS              Bit extraction=0A=
     IBSET              Set bit=0A=
     IEOR               Exclusive OR=0A=
     IOR                Inclusive OR=0A=
     ISHFT              Logical shift=0A=
     ISHFTC             Circular shift=0A=
     NOT                Logical complement=0A=
=0A=
</PRE>
<P>Transfer function, as in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>            <SPAN class=3D"kt">INTEGER</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"nb">TRANSFER</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s1">'abcd'</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>(replaces part of EQUIVALENCE)</P>
<P>Subroutines</P>
<PRE>     DATE_AND_TIME      Obtain date and/or time=0A=
     MVBITS             Copies bits=0A=
     RANDOM_NUMBER      Returns pseudorandom numbers=0A=
     RANDOM_SEED        Access to seed=0A=
     SYSTEM_CLOCK       Access to system clock=0A=
     CPU_TIME           Returns processor time in seconds=0A=
</PRE>
<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Data_transfer">Data =
transfer</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: Data =
transfer"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D60">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<P>(This is a subset only of the actual features and, exceptionally, =
lower case=20
is used in the code examples.)</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Formatted_input.2Foutput">Formatted=20
input/output</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Formatted input/output" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D61">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>These examples illustrate various forms of I/O lists with some simple =
formats=20
(see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Edit_d=
escriptors">below</A>):</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>             <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">real</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">dimension</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">20</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>   <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">word</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s2">"(i10)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN>     <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(10f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(3f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s2">"(a10)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN>     <SPAN class=3D"n">word</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">5</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">14</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(3f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"nb">sqrt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Variables, but not expressions, are equally valid in input statements =
using=20
the <CODE>read</CODE> statement:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(i10)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>If an array appears as an item, it is treated as if the elements were =

specified in array element order.</P>
<P>Any pointers in an I/O list must be associated with a target, and =
transfer=20
takes place between the file and the targets.</P>
<P>An item of derived type is treated as if the components were =
specified in the=20
same order as in the type declaration, so</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(8f10.5)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"c">! types point and triangle</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>has the same effect as the statement</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(8f10.5)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">p</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">&amp;</SPAN>=0A=
                              <SPAN class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">x</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">c</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">%</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">y</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>An object in an I/O list is not permitted to be of a derived type =
that has a=20
pointer component at any level of component selection.</P>
<P>Note that a zero-sized array may occur as an item in an I/O list. =
Such an=20
item corresponds to no actual data transfer.</P>
<P>The format specification may also be given in the form of a character =

expression:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D*</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">parameter</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">form</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(f10.3)"</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">print </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">form</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">q</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>or as an asterisk=E2=80=94this is a type of I/O known as =
<I>list-directed</I> I/O=20
(see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#List-d=
irected_I.2FO">below</A>),=20
in which the format is defined by the computer system:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s2">"Square-root of q =3D =
"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"nb">sqrt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">q</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Input/output operations are used to transfer data between the storage =
of an=20
executing program and an external medium, specified by a <I>unit =
number</I>.=20
However, two I/O statements, <CODE>print</CODE> and a variant of=20
<CODE>read</CODE>, do not reference any unit number: this is referred to =
as=20
terminal I/O. Otherwise the form is:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN>     <SPAN =
class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">q</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nunit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">q</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>where <CODE>unit=3D</CODE> is optional. The value may be any =
nonnegative=20
integer allowed by the system for this purpose (but 0, 5 and 6 often =
denote the=20
error, keyboard and terminal, respectively).</P>
<P>An asterisk is a variant=E2=80=94again from the keyboard:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"(f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">q</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>A read with a unit specifier allows <A title=3D"Exception handling" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exception_handling">exception=20
handling</A>:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nunit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(3f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">c</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">if</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">then</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!     Successful read - continue execution.</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">else</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!     Error condition - take appropriate action.</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"k">call </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">error</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">end if</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>There a second type of formatted output statement, the =
<CODE>write</CODE>=20
statement:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">write</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">nout</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"(10f10.3)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Internal_files">Internal =
files</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Internal files"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D62">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>These allow format conversion between various representations to be =
carried=20
out by the program in a storage area defined within the program =
itself.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">dimension</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">30</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>         <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">ival</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>                        <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">key</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">30</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>              <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">buffer</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">6</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">dimension</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">parameter</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">form</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(30i1)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(15i2)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(10i3)"</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"(a30,i1)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"n">buffer</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">key</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">buffer</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">form</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">key</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">))</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">ival</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">30</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">key</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>If an internal file is a scalar, it has a single record whose length =
is that=20
of the scalar. If it is an array, its elements, in array element order, =
are=20
treated as successive records of the file and each has length that of an =
array=20
element. An example using a <CODE>write</CODE> statement is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>           <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">day</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">real</SPAN>              <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">cash</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">50</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">line</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!   write into line</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">write</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">line</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(a, i2, a, f8.2, a)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"s2">"Takings for day "</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">day</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">" are "</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">cash</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s2">" =
dollars"</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>that might write</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"n">Takings</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">for</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">day</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"mi">3</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">are</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"mi">432</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mf">9.15</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">dollars</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"List-directed_I.2FO">List-directed =

I/O</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
List-directed I/O"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D63">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>An example of a read without a specified format for input is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>               <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">real</SPAN>                  <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">complex</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">dimension</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">field</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">logical</SPAN>               <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">flag</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">12</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>     <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">title</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>      <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">word</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">field</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">flag</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">title</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">word</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>If this reads the input record</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE><SPAN class=3D"mi">10</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mf">6.4</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mf">1.0</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mf">0.0</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mf">2.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mf">0.0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">t</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">test</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>(in which blanks are used as separators), then <CODE>i</CODE>,=20
<CODE>a</CODE>, <CODE>field</CODE>, <CODE>flag</CODE>, and =
<CODE>title</CODE>=20
will acquire the values 10, 6.4, (1.0,0.0) and (2.0,0.0), =
<CODE>.true.</CODE>=20
and <CODE>test</CODE> respectively, while <CODE>word</CODE> remains=20
unchanged.</P>
<P>Quotation marks or apostrophes are required as delimiters for a =
string that=20
contains a blank.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Non-advancing_I.2FO">Non-advancing =

I/O</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Non-advancing I/O"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D64">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>This is a form of reading and writing without always advancing the =
file=20
position to ahead of the next record. Whereas an advancing I/O statement =
always=20
repositions the file after the last record accessed, a non-advancing I/O =

statement performs no such repositioning and may therefore leave the =
file=20
positioned within a record.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">key</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">u</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(a3)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">advance</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"no"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">size</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">key</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">if</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">=3D=3D</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"mi">0</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">then</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">else</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!    key is not in one record</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">key</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">s</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s2">""</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">end if</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>A non-advancing read might read the first few characters of a record =
and a=20
normal read the remainder.</P>
<P>In order to write a prompt to a terminal screen and to read from the =
next=20
character position on the screen without an intervening line-feed, we =
can=20
write</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">write</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"(a)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">advance</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"no"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s2">"enter next prime number:"</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"(i10)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">prime_number</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Non-advancing I/O is for external files, and is not available for=20
list-directed I/O.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Edit_descriptors">Edit =
descriptors</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: Edit =
descriptors"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D65">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>It is possible to specify that an edit descriptor be repeated a =
specified=20
number of times, using a <I>repeat count</I>::</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"mi">10</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">f12</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">.</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">3</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The slash edit descriptor (see <A =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortran_95_language_features#Contro=
l_edit_descriptors">below</A>)=20
may have a repeat count, and a repeat count can also apply to a group of =
edit=20
descriptors, enclosed in parentheses, with nesting:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(2(2i5,2f8.2))"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">3</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">),</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Entire format specifications can be repeated:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(10i8)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">200</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>writes 10 integers, each occupying 8 character positions, on each of =
20 lines=20
(repeating the format specification advances to the next line).</P>
<H4><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Data_edit_descriptors">Data edit=20
descriptors</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Data edit descriptors" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D66">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H4>
<DIV>
<UL>
  <LI>Integer: <CODE>iW iW.M</CODE></LI>
  <LI>Real: <CODE>fW.D esW.D esW.DeE</CODE></LI>
  <LI>Complex: pairs of <CODE>f</CODE> or <CODE>es</CODE> edit =
descriptors</LI>
  <LI>Logical: <CODE>lW</CODE></LI>
  <LI>Character: <CODE>a aW</CODE></LI>
  <LI>Derived types: are edited by the appropriate sequence of edit =
descriptors=20
  corresponding to the intrinsic types of the ultimate components of the =
derived=20
  type.=20
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">type</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">public</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">string</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>   <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"n">length</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">20</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">word</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">end type </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">string</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">type</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">string</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">text</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"(i2, a)"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">text</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV></LI></UL></DIV>
<H4><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Control_edit_descriptors">Control =
edit=20
descriptors</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Control edit descriptors" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D67">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H4>
<P><I>Control edit descriptors setting conditions</I>:</P>
<DIV>
<UL>
  <LI>The <CODE>ss</CODE> (sign suppress) edit descriptor suppresses =
leading=20
  plus signs. To switch on plus sign printing, the <CODE>sp</CODE> (sign =
print)=20
  descriptor is used. The <CODE>s</CODE> edit descriptor restores the =
option to=20
  the processor.</LI>
  <LI>This descriptor remains in force for the remainder of the format=20
  specification, unless another of them is met.</LI></UL></DIV>
<P><I>Control edit descriptors for immediate processing</I>:</P>
<DIV>
<UL>
  <LI>Tabulation: <CODE>tN trN tlN</CODE>=20
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">fmt</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"(t3,i4, tl4,i1, =
i2)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">k</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV></LI>
  <LI>New records: <CODE>/ N/</CODE>=20
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(i5,i3,/,i5,i3,i2)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">j</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">k</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">l</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">m</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
  <P>Note that</P>
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"(i5,4/,i5)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">j</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
  separates the two values by three blank records.</LI>
  <LI>Colon editing: <CODE>&nbsp;:</CODE>=20
  <P>terminates format control if there are no further items in an I/O =
list.</P>
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">print</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"s2">"( i5, :, =
/, i5, :, /, i5)"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">l</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">),</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">n</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
  stops new records if <CODE>n</CODE> equals 1 or 2.</LI></UL></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Unformatted_I.2FO">Unformatted =
I/O</SPAN><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Unformatted I/O"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D68">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>This type of I/O should be used only in cases where the records are =
generated=20
by a program on one computer, to be read back on the same computer or =
another=20
computer using the same internal number representations:</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">open</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">file</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s1">'test'</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">form</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s1">'unformatted'</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">4</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">q</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">write</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nout</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>  <SPAN class=3D"c">! no fmt=3D</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Direct-access_files">Direct-access =

files</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A title=3D"Edit section: =
Direct-access files"=20
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D69">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>This form of I/O is also known as random access or indexed I/O. Here, =
all the=20
records have the same length, and each record is identified by an index =
number.=20
It is possible to write, read, or re-write any specified record without =
regard=20
to position.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> =
<SPAN class=3D"k">parameter</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">nunit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">length</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">100</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">real</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">dimension</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">length</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>            <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">real</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">dimension</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">length</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">+</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">*</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">length</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>                            <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">rec_length</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">inquire</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">iolength</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">rec_length</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">open</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nunit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"nb">access</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"direct"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">recl</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">rec_length</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">status</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"scratch"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">action</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"readwrite"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!      Write array b to direct-access file in record =
14</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">write</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nunit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">rec</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">14</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">b</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!      Read the array back into array a</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">read</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nunit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">rec</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">14</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"p">:</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">do </SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">length</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">/</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">2</SPAN>=0A=
      <SPAN class=3D"n">a</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">i</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">i</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">end do</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"c">!      Replace modified record</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">write</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nunit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">rec</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">14</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">a</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>The file must be an external file and list-directed formatting and=20
non-advancing I/O are unavailable.</P>
<H2><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" =
id=3D"Operations_on_external_files">Operations on=20
external files</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: Operations on external files" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D70">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H2>
<P>Once again, this is an overview only.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"File_positioning_statements">File =
positioning=20
statements</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: File positioning statements" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D71">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<DIV>
<UL>
  <LI>The <CODE>backspace</CODE> statement:=20
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">backspace</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">u</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">[,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">])</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"c">! where [ ] means =
optional</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV></LI>
  <LI>The <CODE>rewind</CODE> statement:=20
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">rewind</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">[,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">])</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV></LI>
  <LI>The <CODE>endfile</CODE> statement:=20
  <DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"n">endfile</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">[,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">])</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV></LI></UL></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"The_open_statement">The =
<CODE>open</CODE>=20
statement</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: The open statement" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D72">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>The statement is used to connect an external file to a unit, create a =
file=20
that is preconnected, or create a file and connect it to a unit. The =
syntax=20
is</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">open</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">status</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">st</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">action</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">act</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">[,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">olist</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">])</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>where <CODE>olist</CODE> is a list of optional specifiers. The =
specifiers may=20
appear in any order.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">open</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"k">file</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"cities"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">status</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"new"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"nb">access</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"direct"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN>  <SPAN =
class=3D"p">&amp;</SPAN>=0A=
         <SPAN class=3D"n">action</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"s2">"readwrite"</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">recl</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mi">100</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>Other specifiers are <CODE>form</CODE> and <CODE>position</CODE>.</P>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"The_close_statement">The =
<CODE>close</CODE>=20
statement</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: The close statement" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D73">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>This is used to disconnect a file from a unit.</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">close</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">u</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">[,</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">]</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">[,</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">status</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">st</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">])</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>as in</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">close</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">iostat</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ios</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">status</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"s2">"delete"</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<H3><SPAN class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"The_inquire_statement">The=20
<CODE>inquire</CODE> statement</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection"><SPAN =
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">[</SPAN><A=20
title=3D"Edit section: The inquire statement" =
href=3D"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=3DFortran_95_language_=
features&amp;action=3Dedit&amp;section=3D74">edit</A><SPAN=20
class=3D"mw-editsection-bracket">]</SPAN></SPAN></H3>
<P>At any time during the execution of a program it is possible to =
inquire about=20
the status and attributes of a file using this statement. Using a =
variant of=20
this statement, it is similarly possible to determine the status of a =
unit, for=20
instance whether the unit number exists for that system Another variant =
permits=20
an inquiry about the length of an output list when used to write an =
unformatted=20
record.</P>
<P>For inquire by unit</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>      <SPAN class=3D"k">inquire</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">u</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">ilist</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>or for inquire by file</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">inquire</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"k">file</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">fln</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">ilist</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>or for inquire by I/O list</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"k">inquire</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">iolength</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">length</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">olist</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>As an example</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE>   <SPAN class=3D"kt">logical</SPAN>            <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">ex</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">op</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">character</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"nb">len</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">11</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">)</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">nam</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">acc</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">seq</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">frm</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"kt">integer</SPAN>            <SPAN =
class=3D"kd">::</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">irec</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">nr</SPAN>=0A=
   <SPAN class=3D"k">inquire</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"p">(</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">unit</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"mi">2</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">exist</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">ex</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">opened</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">op</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">name</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">nam</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"nb">access</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">acc</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">sequential</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">seq</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"n">form</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">frm</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN =
class=3D"p">&amp;</SPAN>=0A=
            <SPAN class=3D"n">recl</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">irec</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">,</SPAN> <SPAN class=3D"n">nextrec</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"o">=3D</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"n">nr</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"p">)</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>yields</P>
<DIV class=3D"mw-highlight mw-content-ltr" dir=3D"ltr">
<PRE><SPAN class=3D"n">ex</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"p">.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">true</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">.</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">op</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"p">.</SPAN><SPAN =
class=3D"n">true</SPAN><SPAN class=3D"p">.</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">nam</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"n">cities</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">acc</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"n">DIRECT</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">seq</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"n">NO</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">frm</SPAN>      <SPAN class=3D"n">UNFORMATTED</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">irec</SPAN>     <SPAN class=3D"mi">100</SPAN>=0A=
<SPAN class=3D"n">nr</SPAN>       <SPAN class=3D"mi">1</SPAN>=0A=
</PRE></DIV>
<P>(assuming no intervening read or write operations).</P>
<P>Other specifiers are <CODE>iostat, opened, number, named, formatted,=20
position, action, read, write, readwrite</CODE>.</P>
